<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_armorkit_17.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>Crafted items are a quick way to gain power on a new character, but this shortcut usually means that you have to spend a sizeable amount of Gold for these items early on when they are the most powerful. The most interesting items available come from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a>, but the Engineering Goggles are a very strong choice early into the Expansion.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> provides the most Agility of any available trinket options, making it the strongest of all pre-raid trinkets before having access to celestial gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85787/chestguard-of-earthen-harmony">
<img alt="Chestguard of Earthen Harmony" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chestguard of Earthen Harmony</span></a> is a good option on a new character, especially when you want to save Valor Points to spend on other items.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85822/gloves-of-earthen-harmony">
<img alt="Gloves of Earthen Harmony" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_dungeonmail_c_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gloves of Earthen Harmony</span></a> is a good option on a new character, especially when you want to save Valor Points to spend on other items.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77536/deadly-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Deadly Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deadly Retinal Armor</span></a> offers the unique possibility to use Engineering Tinker's Gear, which is a massive stat boost early on.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> is a very strong trinket option and incredibly easy to obtain if you are an Alchemist.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85830/raiment-of-blood-and-bone">
<img alt="Raiment of Blood and Bone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_raidhunter_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Raiment of Blood and Bone</span></a> becomes an option once raids are cleared and new recipes are discovered. This becomes the new option for fresh characters and replaces <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85787/chestguard-of-earthen-harmony">
<img alt="Chestguard of Earthen Harmony" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chestguard of Earthen Harmony</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85831/raven-lords-gloves">
<img alt="Raven Lord's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_raidhunter_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Raven Lord's Gloves</span></a> becomes an option once raids are cleared and new recipes are discovered. This becomes the new option for fresh characters and replaces <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85822/gloves-of-earthen-harmony">
<img alt="Gloves of Earthen Harmony" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_dungeonmail_c_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gloves of Earthen Harmony</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_cat_trinket08.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Enhancement Shaman Trinkets</span></h2>For trinkets, Enhancement Shamans aim for Agility, Mastery, Haste, or Critical Strike. Generally, two passive trinkets are preferred, but some fights might favor the damage profile of an on-use trinket.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> provides the most Agility of any available trinket options, making it the strongest of all pre-raid trinkets before having access to celestial gear.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86890/terror-in-the-mists">
<img alt="Terror in the Mists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Terror in the Mists</span></a> becomes the strongest pre-raid trinket once celestials become available. Its strength mainly comes from the sheer amount of stats it provides due to its higher item level.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> provides a lot of Mastery and a strong Agility proc, while being very easy to obtain. This makes it a very good choice for pre-raid gearing.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81267/searing-words">
<img alt="Searing Words" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Searing Words</span></a> is just as strong as the Zen Alchemist Stone. It might not look as strong, due to the Critical Strike on the Item. What makes it so strong is the duration of the Agility Proc, covering more of the burst phases.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86791/bottle-of-infinite-stars">
<img alt="Bottle of Infinite Stars" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bottle of Infinite Stars</span></a> is slightly weaker than Searing Words or the Zen Alechmist Stone, but it remains as an easily farmable pre-raid trinket choice.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81125/windswept-pages">
<img alt="Windswept Pages" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Windswept Pages</span></a> is the weakest option available from Heroic Dungeons, but it is still a viable choice if the Darkmoon Card trinket is too expensive.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81265/flashing-steel-talisman">
<img alt="Flashing Steel Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bladestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashing Steel Talisman</span></a> is the strongest active trinket available before raids open. Due to the massive amount of Hit on the trinket, it also allows for more flexible gearing before raids.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as the  <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This effectively means your abilities will never miss, though your regular swings still might.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them. For the vast majority of Raid bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry from behind. Expertise will also add to your Spell Hit. By reaching 7.5% in both Expertise and Hit, you will be able to reach 15% Spell Hit.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>You will try your best to match the sockets gem color whenever possible. The main goal is to stack Agility through your gems, but the extra Hit or Expertise allows for more optimal gearing and reforging. Avoid gemming pure Hit or Expertise, except for Engineering gems. However, if your gear won't allow you to reach your caps, try to gem the rest of the way, trying to match socket colors.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
